Session 290 summary — D-488 leg 7 ruling part 1a is implemented and building:

**Landed (0.11.504, srcversion 96F7DBC45AEA30D203219F7, built clean, NOT yet deployed):** The CAW acquire path now supports an *attested* form where the AG caller passes its published in-core write-authority epoch down to the lock body. In the already-held fast path, reaffirming with the slot's old epoch is now only legal when the caller's published epoch is nonzero and matches the slot (an ordinary reentrant acquire). An own bit with attested epoch 0 — a post-surrender stranded bit, the D-488 orphan — instead takes a new forced READOPT mint: a real CAS that keeps the bit present and writes a fresh epoch (P294-READOPT-MINT), publishing only on definite CAS success and failing closed on anything ambiguous, so the surrendered epoch can never be resurrected as write authority. The mount adopt window is exempt, preserving the sess52 inheritance ruling; all non-AG callers are unchanged via the old unattested entry. The STILL_HELD re-arm's false "reaffirm mints a fresh epoch" comment is corrected — the re-arm now genuinely mints through this path.

